english.DocsShortcut=AgentDock documentation
english.UninstallShortcut=Uninstall AgentDock
english.StartupPageCaption=Startup
english.StartupPageDescription=Choose how AgentDock starts with Windows
english.StartupPageSubCaption=The tray stays a normal user process. Administrator mode applies only to the AgentDock core.
english.StartupOption=Start AgentDock and the tray after signing in
english.ElevatedCoreOption=Run the AgentDock core with administrator privileges (recommended)
english.UpgradeModeCaption=Upgrade or repair
english.UpgradeModeDescription=AgentDock is already installed
english.UpgradeModeSubCaption=Keep the current configuration for a normal upgrade, or open the settings pages when you need to change it.
english.UpgradeKeepSettings=Upgrade and keep all current settings (recommended)
english.UpgradeChangeSettings=Modify startup and connection settings
english.ConnectionPageCaption=Connection
english.ConnectionPageDescription=Choose who can reach AgentDock
english.ConnectionPageSubCaption=Local-only access is the default. Public access is enabled only when you select it explicitly.
english.LocalMode=Local access only (recommended)
english.QuickMode=Create a temporary public URL (refreshes after restart)
english.NamedMode=Use my Cloudflare domain
english.QuickLifecycleNote=Temporary URLs change when Windows or Cloudflare Tunnel restarts. AgentDock refreshes the URL automatically; use the tray menu to regenerate it at any time.
english.FixedPageCaption=Fixed public URL
english.FixedPageDescription=Enter the Cloudflare Tunnel settings
english.FixedPageSubCaption=Enter an HTTPS origin such as https://agent.example.com. The Tunnel Token never appears in process arguments.
